Title:
TTs – Text Transform Shells

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
TTs is a payload builder that generates shellcode loaders executed through Visual Studio’s T4 text templating engine using `TextTransform.exe` and `.tt` files. It embeds XOR-encrypted raw shellcode into a generated C# assembly, compiles it with the .NET Framework C# compiler, and produces a `.tt` template that base64-loads and invokes the assembly. The loader uses the 3lkToShell technique: DynamicMethod JIT spraying to obtain an RWX region in the CLR HostCodeHeap, copying shellcode there, then executing it via a second DynamicMethod from inside a catch handler (SEH second pass). A key goal is avoiding `VirtualAlloc` appearing in the call stack, which can reduce certain user-mode detection opportunities. This is primarily useful for red teams, pentesters, and offensive security researchers exploring LOLBin-style execution paths and .NET/CLR-based in-memory execution.

Technical Focus:
- T4 Text Templates (`.tt`) execution via `TextTransform.exe`
- .NET DynamicMethod JIT spray and CLR HostCodeHeap RWX allocation
- In-memory shellcode staging/execution without `VirtualAlloc` in stack trace
- XOR shellcode encryption and base64 assembly loading
- SEH/catch-handler execution flow (second-pass exception handling)

Use Cases:
- Execute shellcode via a developer tooling binary (`TextTransform.exe`) in environments with Visual Studio components installed
- Prototype and test CLR-based shellcode execution techniques that avoid common allocation APIs
- Generate packaged payloads combining `.tt` templates, required dependencies, and a compiled loader assembly
- Research/detection engineering: build test cases for monitoring T4 template execution and suspicious DynamicMethod behavior

Keywords:
TextTransform.exe, T4, .tt, Text Template Transformation Toolkit, Visual Studio, LOLBin, C# loader, .NET Framework, CSC.exe, DynamicMethod, JIT spray, HostCodeHeap, CLR internals, RWX memory, shellcode loader, SEH, catch handler, base64 load, XOR encryption, in-memory execution